-- #347: the wilds' nodes planted only where a walker can get to them.
--
-- The wild land's reach test flooded out from the rural edge over cells 25
-- across, testing the slope only at the cells' centres. The ridged land has
-- crests steeper than the cliff (1.2) for under a unit, and where they close
-- round a hollow nothing walks in or out: the flood stepped over them, and
-- some wild nodes stood in such pockets. It also flooded past the world's
-- edge, and round it out of pockets the edge closes. The Flint client's walk
-- graph said so (#280): no way there, so a gatherer shunned the node and a
-- player who clicked one was told "Too steep" at the rim.
--
-- Now the flood goes along the line between two cells' centres, tested as
-- the walk graph tests a line (`rules::ground::slope_lets_through`, shared by
-- both), keeps inside the world, and a node's own spot must be reached from
-- its cell's centre or a reached neighbour's (`wilds::Land::reached`). Half
-- the iron's high ground was in pockets (2392 suited cells to 1168); of all
-- the wild cells, 57% were reached and now 54% are.
--
-- The set of reached cells changes, so every wild resource draws from a
-- different list and every wild node moves, as at #340. Nothing outside the
-- wilds moves. So this deletes the rows the plan no longer has, by id, and
-- inserts the new ones. Nothing a player owns is a node; a node half
-- gathered starts over.
--
-- The rows come from the ignored test `print_node_replan`, and
-- `the_migration_writes_the_default_plan` checks the plan still matches.
--
-- deleted and inserted, 14127 each, all in the wilderness:
--   clay_bank: 393
--   copper_vein: 995
--   fallen_branches: 2986
--   iron_vein: 796
--   old_growth: 5972
--   reed_bed: 596
--   rock_outcrop: 1991
--   tin_vein: 398

